          "filename": "Hook Head lighthouse (1) - geograph.org.uk - 202252.jpg",
          "caption": "Hook Head lighthouse (1) \nThe tower of Hook Head lighthouse was built sometime about 1172 as an aid to navigation.  It fell into disuse but was re-established in about 1667.  It was powered by coal-gas from 1871, vapourised paraffin from 1911 and electricity from 1972.",
